{
  "info": {
    "name": "OAN Registry - local",
    "description": "End-to-end tests for the OAN Registry running from network-layer/registry/docker-compose.yml.\n\nRun the whole collection top to bottom (Postman Runner or newman) - requests share state through collection variables: the first request stamps a run_id, the token request stores the bearer, and the create requests store osids.\n\nEvery request has assertions, and the run cleans up after itself.\n\nVerified against sunbird-rc-core v2.0.0 with authentication_enabled=true and the elasticsearch search provider. Where real behaviour differs from API_SPECIFICATION.md, the request description says so.\n\nCookies are disabled for every request in this collection. The registry issues a JSESSIONID on the first token-authenticated call, and that session cookie is accepted afterwards INSTEAD of a bearer token - so any client with a cookie jar (Postman, newman, a browser) stays authenticated and the no-token tests below would wrongly pass. Real API clients such as ONIX do not keep cookies, so disabling them is also the honest test.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "registry_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081"
    },
    {
      "key": "keycloak_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "es_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:9200"
    },
    {
      "key": "realm",
      "value": "sunbird-rc"
    },
    {
      "key": "client_id",
      "value": "registry-frontend"
    },
    {
      "key": "no_user",
      "value": "no-user"
    },
    {
      "key": "no_password",
      "value": "no-user-password"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "run_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "provider_osid",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "no_osid",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "invited_osid",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "bad_issuer_token",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health check",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/health",
        "description": "Confirms the registry is up and that its elasticsearch and keycloak checks pass.\n\nAlso stamps a run_id used by every later request, so the collection can be re-run without colliding on participant_id (a deleted record's row physically remains, so re-using an id returns 500)."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const r = pm.response.json().result;",
              "pm.test('registry healthy', () => pm.expect(r.healthy).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('elasticsearch healthy', () => pm.expect(r.checks.find(c => c.name.includes('elastic')).healthy).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('keycloak healthy', () => pm.expect(r.checks.find(c => c.name.includes('keycloak')).healthy).to.be.true);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('run_id', Date.now());"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Participant API surface (swagger)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/docs/swagger.json",
        "description": "Lists the endpoints the registry generated from schemas/Participant.json. Proves the schema was loaded at boot."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const paths = Object.keys(pm.response.json().paths);",
              "pm.test('Participant endpoints exist', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(paths).to.include('/api/v1/Participant');",
              "  pm.expect(paths).to.include('/api/v1/Participant/search');",
              "  pm.expect(paths).to.include('/api/v1/Participant/{entityId}');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Get Network Operator token",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-Forwarded-Host",
            "value": "keycloak:8080"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-Forwarded-Proto",
            "value": "http"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{keycloak_url}}/auth/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
        "description": "The X-Forwarded-* headers are required when calling Keycloak from the host: without them the token's `iss` is http://localhost:8080/... which does not match what the registry expects internally (http://keycloak:8080/auth/realms/sunbird-rc), and every write comes back 401.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "urlencoded",
          "urlencoded": [
            {
              "key": "client_id",
              "value": "{{client_id}}",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "key": "username",
              "value": "{{no_user}}",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "key": "password",
              "value": "{{no_password}}",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "key": "grant_type",
              "value": "password",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', b.access_token);",
              "const claims = JSON.parse(atob(b.access_token.split('.')[1].replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/')));",
              "pm.test('token carries network_operator role', () => pm.expect(claims.realm_access.roles).to.include('network_operator'));",
              "pm.test('issuer matches what the registry expects', () => pm.expect(claims.iss).to.eql('http://keycloak:8080/auth/realms/sunbird-rc'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Create the Network Operator's own record",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant",
        "description": "The Network Operator is a Participant too, so it can be resolved like anyone else.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"participant_id\": \"no-{{run_id}}\",\n  \"display_name\": \"OAN Network Operator\",\n  \"roles\": [\n    \"network_operator\"\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"domain\": \"network\",\n  \"record_version\": 1,\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T10:00:00Z\",\n  \"endpoint_url\": \"https://no.example.com/onix\",\n  \"endpoint_type\": \"onix\",\n  \"signing_public_key\": \"MCowBQYDK2VwAyEA3fS8bYhWEfmM7Zjk9x0EhAmvQKp3fMHXqTiA5xL1Qmw=\",\n  \"signing_algorithm\": \"ed25519\",\n  \"key_valid_from\": \"2026-08-19T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"key_valid_until\": \"2027-08-19T00:00:00Z\"\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('SUCCESSFUL', () => pm.expect(b.params.status).to.eql('SUCCESSFUL'));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('no_osid', b.result.Participant.osid);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Create a Provider",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant",
        "description": "Only a token holding `admin` or `network_operator` can write to Participant - that is the `roles` list in the schema's _osConfig. There is no self-registration path.\n\nSaves the returned osid as {{provider_osid}} for every later request.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"participant_id\": \"provider-{{run_id}}\",\n  \"display_name\": \"Provider A Agri Services\",\n  \"roles\": [\n    \"provider\"\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"domain\": \"weather\",\n  \"record_version\": 1,\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T10:00:00Z\",\n  \"endpoint_url\": \"https://providera.example.com/onix\",\n  \"endpoint_type\": \"onix\",\n  \"signing_public_key\": \"MCowBQYDK2VwAyEA3fS8bYhWEfmM7Zjk9x0EhAmvQKp3fMHXqTiA5xL1Qmw=\",\n  \"signing_algorithm\": \"ed25519\",\n  \"key_valid_from\": \"2026-08-19T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"key_valid_until\": \"2027-08-19T00:00:00Z\"\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('SUCCESSFUL', () => pm.expect(b.params.status).to.eql('SUCCESSFUL'));",
              "pm.test('returns an osid', () => pm.expect(b.result.Participant.osid).to.be.a('string'));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('provider_osid', b.result.Participant.osid);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Force elasticsearch refresh (dev only)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{es_url}}/_refresh",
        "description": "Dev-only. /search is served by elasticsearch, which refreshes about once a second, so a search fired immediately after a write can read stale data. This forces the refresh so the searches below are deterministic. Not something a real client would call."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Search - one Provider by participant_id",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant/search",
        "description": "This endpoint is public - it is allow-listed in the registry's security config, so no token is needed. Do not send an empty `Authorization: Bearer` header: Spring's OAuth2 filter rejects it with 401 before the permit rule is reached.\n\nThe response is an object - `{ data: [...], totalCount: n }` - not a bare array. `totalCount` reads 0 with the elasticsearch provider; use `data.length`.\n\nRecords come back complete, including `endpoints` and `keys`, which is what makes this the resolve call ONIX will use.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"participant_id\": {\n      \"eq\": \"provider-{{run_id}}\"\n    }\n  }\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
              "pm.test('exactly one match', () => pm.expect(d.length).to.eql(1));",
              "pm.test('active', () => pm.expect(d[0].status).to.eql('active'));",
              "pm.test('key material is returned', () => pm.expect(d[0].signing_public_key).to.be.a('string'));",
              "pm.test('endpoint is returned', () => pm.expect(d[0].endpoint_url).to.be.a('string'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Search - all active Providers",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant/search",
        "description": "Filters combine with AND.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"roles\": {\n      \"contains\": \"provider\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"eq\": \"active\"\n    }\n  }\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
              "pm.test('includes this run\\'s provider', () => pm.expect(d.map(r => r.participant_id)).to.include('provider-' + pm.collectionVariables.get('run_id')));",
              "pm.test('all returned are active providers', () => d.forEach(r => { pm.expect(r.status).to.eql('active'); pm.expect(r.roles).to.include('provider'); }));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Search - active Providers in one domain",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant/search",
        "description": "Domain-scoped discovery: which Providers serve weather.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"roles\": {\n      \"contains\": \"provider\"\n    },\n    \"domain\": {\n      \"eq\": \"weather\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"eq\": \"active\"\n    }\n  }\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
              "pm.test('includes this run\\'s provider', () => pm.expect(d.map(r => r.participant_id)).to.include('provider-' + pm.collectionVariables.get('run_id')));",
              "pm.test('all in the weather domain', () => d.forEach(r => pm.expect(r.domain).to.eql('weather')));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Search - all inactive Providers (none yet)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant/search",
        "description": "Nothing has been suspended yet, so this run's provider must not appear. An empty result is 200 with `data: []`, never a 404.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"roles\": {\n      \"contains\": \"provider\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"eq\": \"inactive\"\n    }\n  }\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
              "pm.test('this run\\'s provider is not here yet', () => pm.expect(d.map(r => r.participant_id)).to.not.include('provider-' + pm.collectionVariables.get('run_id')));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Search - no match returns an empty list",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant/search",
        "description": "Confirms a miss is an empty list and not an error.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"participant_id\": {\n      \"eq\": \"does-not-exist-{{run_id}}\"\n    }\n  }\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('empty', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.length).to.eql(0));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Get a Participant by osid",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant/{{provider_osid}}",
        "description": "Reads straight from postgres, so it is immediately consistent - unlike /search, which goes through elasticsearch. A token is required here even though /search is public."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('right record', () => pm.expect(b.participant_id).to.eql('provider-' + pm.collectionVariables.get('run_id')));",
              "pm.test('active', () => pm.expect(b.status).to.eql('active'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "List Participants created by this token",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant",
        "description": "Returns the records owned by the caller - the creator is stored as osOwner. Since the Network Operator created both records in this run, both come back."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('at least the two records from this run', () => pm.expect(b.data.length).to.be.at.least(2));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Suspend a Provider (PUT, partial - merge)",
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant/{{provider_osid}}",
        "description": "PUT is a field-level MERGE, not a full replace - verified against this deployment. Fields present in the body are overwritten, fields omitted keep their stored value, and validation runs on the merged document (so omitting a required field is fine). Arrays are replaced wholesale, not appended to, and a field can only be cleared by sending it explicitly.\n\nThis request therefore sends only what changes - osid, status, record_version, updated_at - and the assertions below prove the untouched fields survived. Note the API specification calls PUT a full replace; that is not what the running registry does.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"osid\": \"{{provider_osid}}\",\n  \"status\": \"inactive\",\n  \"record_version\": 2,\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T12:00:00Z\"\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('SUCCESSFUL', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().params.status).to.eql('SUCCESSFUL'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Confirm the suspension (get by osid)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant/{{provider_osid}}",
        "description": "Checked via GET rather than /search because this read is immediately consistent."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('inactive', () => pm.expect(b.status).to.eql('inactive'));",
              "pm.test('version bumped', () => pm.expect(b.record_version).to.eql(2));",
              "pm.test('endpoint survived the partial update', () => pm.expect(b.endpoint_url).to.be.a('string'));",
              "pm.test('signing key survived the partial update', () => pm.expect(b.signing_public_key).to.be.a('string'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Force elasticsearch refresh (dev only)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{es_url}}/_refresh",
        "description": "Dev-only. /search is served by elasticsearch, which refreshes about once a second, so a search fired immediately after a write can read stale data. This forces the refresh so the searches below are deterministic. Not something a real client would call."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Search - inactive Providers now finds it",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": "{{registry_url}}/api/v1/Participant/search",
        "description": "The suspended Provider is now visible as inactive - a suspended participant is still resolvable, just not active.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"roles\": {\n      \"contains\": \"provider\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"eq\": \"inactive\"\n    }\n  }\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
              "pm.test('this run\\'s provider is now inactive', () => pm.expect(d.map(r => r.participant_id)).to.include('provider-' + pm.collectionVariables.get('run_id')));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "protocolProfileBehavior": {
        "disableCookies": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Reactivate the Provider (PUT, full body)",
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
