        },
        "description": "The schema sets `additionalProperties: false`, so a field that is not declared is rejected instead of silently stored. Without it, `endpointurl` would persist as its own column and the record would resolve with no endpoint - a silent failure for anything relying on the registry for endpoints or key material.\n\nThe registry's own system fields (osid, osOwner, osCreatedAt, osUpdatedAt, osCreatedBy, osUpdatedBy, _status) are declared in the schema for this reason: PUT validates the MERGED document, which carries them, so leaving them undeclared makes every update fail with `extraneous key [osUpdatedAt] is not permitted`."
